{
  "version": 1,
  "_note": "Provided-model manifest for the Sunfront build (specs/assets.md). 'dimensions' are the model extents [width, height, depth] and are the on-field relative-scale contract. 'kind' is 'rigid' (parts on named joints) or 'skinned' (linear-blend skinning). 'clips' maps a game role to the animation clip name to play. A destroyed unit is not animated — it flashes white a few times and is removed (specs/units.md), so there is no death clip. A unit's 'muzzle' names which provided muzzle-flash effect (see 'effects') the build plays while it fires, or null for melee and support units that fire no weapon. Per-model 'parts'/'joints' lists (including each firing unit's muzzle joint) are added with each model.",
  "effects": {
    "_note": "Provided muzzle-flash particle systems, authored by the sunfront-muzzle-* particle cases and played via @test-cabinet/particle-runtime (its 'three' binding) while a unit fires (specs/assets.md). Each is a looping system.json the build simulates live, anchored to the firing unit's muzzle joint and oriented along the barrel. A unit's 'muzzle' key selects one of these; melee and support units have muzzle: null.",
    "small-arms": "effects/muzzle-small-arms.json",
    "cannon": "effects/muzzle-cannon.json",
    "lance": "effects/muzzle-lance.json"
  },
  "units": {
